Subject: [PATCH 6/8] docs: the shell, the rail and the board, written down
 where they are looked up

CLAUDE.md, product.md, design-system.md, motion.md and the frontend rules
now describe the shell that exists rather than the one phase 8 left. The
reasoning lives in docs/ and ADR-0027/0028; the obligations live in
.claude/rules/frontend.md, which gained the short imperative form: the
shell is a frame and knows no domain, the rail is composed by the page and
never by a parallel route, an empty rail is an absent column, only the
workspace animates, scroll belongs to the document, and below lg the
portal is phase 8.

FASE85ESTADO.md records what a phase document is for: what the local Next
docs changed about the plan before any code was written, the three defects
a real browser found that jsdom could not, the false overflow that headless
Chromium's 500px window minimum nearly turned into a bug report, and the
debt this phase is knowingly leaving -- chiefly that no one has yet read
the portal logged in, because the no-Docker fallback serves migrations and
RLS but not PostgREST or auth.

Counts refreshed from Vitest, not from grep: 1259 tests in 67 files.

